{
  "_comment": "Mac native .mcp.json — paths + Redis DNS resolved for Mac. Reviewer audit 2026-05-23 caught Docker DNS (redis://redis:6379) + /opt/ paths in master .mcp.json. start-officer-mac.sh will copy this to .mcp.json on first run (and deep-merge with instance/agents/<officer>/mcp.json if drives_computer=true). MCP hygiene 2026-07-07 (audit #3a/#16/#17/#18): make restored with env-based bearer auth, linear deleted (granted to zero agents in cabinet/mcp-scope.yml), npx versions pinned, OFFICER_NAME defaults for non-officer sessions. Doctor DEAD-sweep 2026-07-07 (follow-up): vercel dereferences ${VERCEL_TOKEN} — the canonical cabinet/.env name (.env.example + vercel.sh doctrine); VERCEL_API_KEY is the PersonalSource estate name, mapped only inside probe wrappers. neon RESTORED 2026-07-09 per the parked recipe (§14 call #9 seal): Captain provisioned NEON_API_KEY into cabinet/.env (600), entry re-added in BOTH layers lockstep, env-based bearer auth (never argv); polads-ceo + stephie-ceo grants in schg-locked cabinet/mcp-scope.yml were reserved-for-when-wired and now bind.",
  "mcpServers": {
    "neon": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.neon.tech/mcp",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${NEON_API_KEY}" }
    },
    "notion": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@notionhq/notion-mcp-server"],
      "env": { "NOTION_TOKEN": "${NOTION_API_KEY}" }
    },
    "vercel": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@robinson_ai_systems/vercel-mcp"],
      "env": { "VERCEL_TOKEN": "${VERCEL_TOKEN}" }
    },
    "redis-trigger-channel": {
      "command": "bun",
      "args": ["run", "${CABINET_SOURCE_REPO}/cabinet/channels/redis-trigger-channel/index.ts"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}", "REDIS_URL": "redis://localhost:6379" }
    },
    "cabinet-comms": {
      "command": "python3.12",
      "args": ["${CABINET_SOURCE_REPO}/framework/comms/mcp/server.py"],
      "env": { "COMMS_MCP_TRANSPORT": "stdio" }
    },
    "library": {
      "command": "bun",
      "args": ["run", "${CABINET_SOURCE_REPO}/cabinet/channels/library-mcp/index.ts"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "make": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://eu2.make.com/mcp/stateless",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${MAKE_MCP_TOKEN}" }
    },
    "_comment_captain_layer": "Below: Captain-layer tools (screen memory, browser hands, native Mac hands). Wired via setup-mac.sh Steps 9-12. Officer access gated by per-officer tools: allowlist in presets/work/agents/*.md — CoS sees everything; CTO/COO see playwright; others request via CoS.",
    "screenpipe": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "screenpipe-mcp@0.18.14"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "chrome_devtools": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "chrome-devtools-mcp@1.5.0", "--browserUrl", "http://127.0.0.1:9222"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "playwright": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@playwright/mcp@0.0.77"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "cua": {
      "command": "cua-driver",
      "args": ["mcp", "--claude-code-computer-use-compat"],
      "env": {
        "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}",
        "CUA_MODEL_BACKEND": "${CUA_MODEL_BACKEND:-anthropic}",
        "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"
      }
    }
  }
}
